description: Copper clearance and track width discipline
alwaysApply: true
---

# Clearance

- Start from the fab's minimum (0.15 mm track/clearance for a standard 2-layer run) and only go
  below it after the fab confirms it in writing.
- Power tracks are sized from current, not from habit: 1 A ≈ 0.5 mm of 35 µm copper.
- Never let clearance drift silently to satisfy a single stubborn net — move the part or add a
  layer. A board that only just passes DRC will fail at another fab.
- Record the chosen rules in the project file, so the next revision starts from the same numbers.
